# Accepted vulnerabilities, read by every Trivy scan (CI image job, release). Each entry needs a
# reason and an expiry (exp:YYYY-MM-DD); after it the scan fails again. This file must be empty at
# the security gates before the public demo (Phases 17–19; docs/PROGRESS.md, Follow-ups).

# picomatch 4.0.7 (web/package-lock.json, development tools only: vite, vitest, tinyglobby):
# a denial of service by a crafted glob pattern. No fixed version exists (4.0.7 is the newest
# release, 2026-11-18). Patterns come from the repository's own configuration, never from a user,
# and nothing of it ships in the web image (`npm audit --omit=dev` is clean). Accepted by the
# maintainer on 2026-11-18 until a fix is released; fix it then, do not extend this by default.
# The second id is the same advisory as npm names it (read by tools/npm-audit.mjs).
CVE-2026-112366 exp:2026-12-02
GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf exp:2026-12-02
